      ]
    },
    {
      "ancestors": [
        0
      ],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Returns the bounds on the remaining length of the async iterator.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2373,
            2442
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2447,
            2450
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Specifically, `size_hint()` returns a tuple where the first element",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2455,
            2526
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " is the lower bound, and the second element is the upper bound.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2531,
            2597
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2602,
            2605
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The second half of the tuple that is returned is an <code>[Option]<[usize]></code>.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2610,
            2697
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " A [`None`] here means that either there is no known upper bound, or the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2702,
            2777
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " upper bound is larger than [`usize`].",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2782,
            2823
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2828,
            2831
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # Implementation notes",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2836,
            2862
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2867,
            2870
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " It is not enforced that an async iterator implementation yields the declared",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2875,
            2955
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " number of elements. A buggy async iterator may yield less than the lower bound",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2960,
            3042
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " or more than the upper bound of elements.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3047,
            3092
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3097,
            3100
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `size_hint()` is primarily intended to be used for optimizations such as",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3105,
            3181
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " reserving space for the elements of the async iterator, but must not be",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3186,
            3261
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " trusted to e.g., omit bounds checks in unsafe code. An incorrect",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3266,
            3334
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " implementation of `size_hint()` should not lead to memory safety",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3339,
            3407
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " violations.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3412,
            3427
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3432,
            3435
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " That said, the implementation should provide a correct estimation,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3440,
            3510
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " because otherwise it would be a violation of the trait's protocol.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3515,
            3585
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3590,
            3593
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The default implementation returns <code>(0, [None])</code> which is correct for any",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3598,
            3686
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " async iterator.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3691,
            3710
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "inline",
          "range": [
            3715,
            3724
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        }
